            B.q("sa-m3-7", "sa-identity", "Conditional Access must require MFA for everyone, but if MFA or the federation service breaks, administrators must still be able to get in. What do you recommend?", listOf("Exclude all administrators from Conditional Access", "Two cloud-only emergency access accounts with strong credentials, excluded from the policies and monitored", "Turn off MFA whenever there is an outage", "Give every administrator a backup SMS number"), setOf(1), "Emergency access (break-glass) accounts are a small number of cloud-only accounts kept for when normal sign-in fails. They are excluded from policies that could lock everyone out, protected with strong credentials, and alerts fire whenever they are used.",
                scenario = "After a misconfigured policy locked every admin out for a day, Sablewood Finance, which runs an Android trading-alerts app, wants a safe way back in the next time something goes wrong.",
