            B.q("sa-m3-12", "sa-authorization", "The Android app must upload photos straight to Blob Storage without passing through the API, with access limited to one blob for 15 minutes and signed with Entra credentials, not an account key. What do you recommend?", listOf("Embed the storage account key in the app", "Make the container public", "Have the API issue a user delegation SAS for that one blob, valid for 15 minutes", "A service SAS signed with the account key, valid for a year"), setOf(2), "A shared access signature (SAS) is a signed URL that grants limited access. A user delegation SAS is signed with a key obtained through Microsoft Entra ID rather than the account key, and can be limited to one blob, one permission and a short time.",
                scenario = "Snapquill's Android receipt-scanning app sends large photos through its API, which is slow and expensive. The team wants phones to upload directly, safely.",
                whyWrong = mapOf(
