            // Data: semi-structured and unstructured
            B.q("sa-m3-22", "sa-nonrelational", "Traffic swings from 2,000 to 40,000 request units per second during the day, the peak is known, and the team wants Cosmos DB to scale by itself. Which throughput option fits?", listOf("Serverless", "Manual provisioned throughput at 40,000 RU/s", "Autoscale provisioned throughput with a maximum of 40,000 RU/s", "Manual throughput changed by a script each hour"), setOf(2), "Autoscale scales a container's throughput between 10 percent of a maximum and that maximum, instantly, based on use. You set the maximum to the known peak and pay for the highest level reached each hour.",
