            B.q("sa-m3-28", "sa-data-integration", "Raw data from many sources must be kept as it arrived, then cleaned, then shaped into business-ready tables, all in Delta Lake, so that any step can be rebuilt. What design do you recommend?", listOf("Load everything straight into report tables", "A medallion architecture: bronze for raw, silver for cleaned, gold for business-ready", "A single Azure SQL database", "Keep only the final tables and delete raw files"), setOf(1), "The medallion architecture keeps data in layers. Bronze holds raw data as it came, silver holds cleaned and joined data, and gold holds tables ready for reports. Keeping bronze means you can rebuild later layers after a fix.",
                scenario = "Saltford Telecom's data engineers use Azure Databricks to combine billing, network and Android app usage data. A bug last year corrupted reports, and the raw data had already been thrown away.",
