            B.q("sa-m3-30", "sa-data-integration", "A nightly pipeline copies a 2-billion-row orders table in full and takes too long. Only a few thousand rows change each day. What do you recommend?", listOf("Copy the whole table more often", "Copy only changed rows, using a watermark column such as LastModified or change data capture", "Move the copy to a bigger integration runtime", "Copy the table once a week instead"), setOf(1), "An incremental load copies only rows that changed since the last run. A watermark column, such as a last-modified time, or change data capture, which records inserts, updates and deletes, tells the pipeline which rows to take.",
                scenario = "Hartwell Pharmacy's orders table, written by its Android prescription app, is copied in full every night into the data lake. The copy now runs past 08:00, when reports are due.",
                whyWrong = mapOf(
                    0 to "Running a full copy more often makes the problem worse.",
                    2 to "More power shortens the copy a little but still moves 2 billion rows to get a few thousand.",
                    3 to "Weekly copies make the reports up to a week old.",
